    {
      "candidate": "candidate-1",
      "response": {
        "summary": "One capability, src/modules/assistant-reply, owns the generation policy; the interactive SSE stream and the background job are two runtime channels over it. app/api/assistant-reply/route.ts owns HTTP status/headers and the pre-commit mapping; the module's private stream runtime owns the single AbortController, sliding idle timeout, commit state, in-band post-commit failures, and the one unexpected-failure report. application/generate-reply.ts is provider-neutral and silent, talking to a capability-shaped ReplyModel port whose streamReply resolves on upstream acquisition so startup failures stay pre-commit. The job reuses the same operation but with a total deadline and its own retry/dead-letter mapping, never inheriting stream idle semantics.",
        "tree": [
          {
            "path": "src/instrumentation.ts",
            "purpose": "Sentry/runtime init; keeps telemetry SDK out of domain and application"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/app/(chat)/assistant/page.tsx",
            "purpose": "Route-private composition; imports only modules/assistant-reply/client.ts"
          },
