            "path": "src/modules/assistant/application/generate-reply.ts",
            "purpose": "Framework-neutral, silent generation policy: entitlement/quota, model and system-instruction selection, delta sequencing, complete-vs-truncated terminal decision; shared by stream and job."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/application/ports/reply-generation.ts",
            "purpose": "One-role port: streamReply(request, { signal }): Promise<AsyncIterable<ReplyDelta>> — promise-of-iterable so acquisition can fail before any bytes exist."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/config.ts",
            "purpose": "server-only validated provider environment and credentials; fails on first intentional access, not on a browser import."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/provider/reply-transport.ts",
            "purpose": "The single transport for the remote model service: credentials, acquisition timeout, trace-id correlation, caller signal reaching fetch, provider payload validation, provider envelope to semantic failure mapping."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/provider/reply-generation-adapter.ts",
            "purpose": "Implements the port; keeps provider shapes out of application and public contracts; reports nothing."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/stream/open-reply-stream.ts",
            "purpose": "Stream channel assembly: channel-owned AbortController, request-signal and cancel linking, pre-commit upstream acquisition, body construction, cleanup."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/stream/sse-response.ts",
            "purpose": "SSE framing, commit-state machine, done event, and in-band failure event emission after commit."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/stream/idle-abort.ts",
            "purpose": "Sliding idle timeout bound to the channel AbortController; reset only by provider deltas, never by keep-alive frames."
          },

          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/job/run-reply-generation.ts",
            "purpose": "Job-native policy: own whole-run deadline, attempt budget with bounded backoff, retry/drop/dead-letter classification per semantic code."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/server/composition.ts",
            "purpose": "Wires provider client, reporter, and clock into the smallest dependency object each caller needs."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/client/reply-stream-client.ts",
            "purpose": "client-only browser fetch + SSE reader; own AbortController for cancel propagation; validates each event against the published union."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/client/use-reply-stream.ts",
            "purpose": "React async lifecycle: accumulated text plus terminal state (done | error(code) | aborted)."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/stream.ts",
            "purpose": "Streaming contract: openReplyStream, classifyReplyStreamFailure (the public classifier HTTP needs), StreamEvent."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/job.ts",
            "purpose": "Worker contract: runReplyGeneration and ReplyJobOutcome (complete | retry(afterMs) | dead_letter(code))."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/assistant/client.ts",
            "purpose": "Browser-safe surface: useReplyStream and the StreamEvent contract."
          },
          {
            "path": "app/api/assistant/reply/route.ts",
            "purpose": "POST stream channel: route-local body schema, authentication and identity, calls stream.ts, maps pre-commit failures to status/headers, reports the unexpected case once, returns the committed Response."
          },
          {
            "path": "app/api/jobs/assistant-reply/route.ts",
            "purpose": "Queue callback: signature verification before trusting payload, durable idempotency by job id, explicit privileged identity, calls job.ts and maps the outcome to the queue's retry contract."
          },
          {
            "path": "app/(app)/assistant/page.tsx",
            "purpose": "Route-private composition of the assistant screen."
          },
          {
            "path": "app/(app)/assistant/_components/reply-panel.tsx",
            "purpose": "Route-private UI consuming client.ts only; not promoted to a module ui/ segment because it is not reused."
          },
          {
            "path": "instrumentation.ts",
            "purpose": "Reporter/SDK initialization per runtime; domain and application import no telemetry SDK."
          }
        ],
        "flows": [
          "Happy stream: reply-panel.tsx -> client.ts useReplyStream -> POST /api/assistant/reply (browser AbortController signal) -> route validates body with its local schema and authenticates, building identity (actor, roles, tenant, requestId, traceId) -> stream.ts openReplyStream -> server/stream/open-reply-stream.ts creates channel ctl, links request.signal and the stream cancel(reason) callback -> application/generate-reply.ts -> port streamReply -> reply-generation-adapter -> reply-transport fetch(ctl.signal); acquisition is awaited BEFORE the Response exists -> route returns new Response(handle.body, {status:200, content-type text/event-stream, cache-control no-cache no-transform, x-accel-buffering no}) = commit -> sse-response pumps data:{type:chunk,id,data} per delta, resetting the sliding idle timer on each provider delta only -> data:{type:done} -> close -> finally clears timer, removes the signal listener, releases the provider reader.",
          "Pre-commit failure: reply-transport maps provider 429 to rate_limited, provider 5xx/network/timeout to unavailable, provider 401/403 to unavailable (our misconfiguration, never surfaced as caller unauthorized), malformed payload to contract; the failure rejects openReplyStream before any Response -> route maps via classifyReplyStreamFailure: validation 400, forbidden 403, rate_limited 429, unavailable 503, acquisition timeout 504, contract/unknown 500 -> route reports the unexpected case exactly once with request/trace context and never echoes provider text.",
          "Post-commit failure: adapter maps the provider error to a semantic code and throws -> sse-response emits data:{type:error,code:<same semantic code>} in band and closes with no trailing done -> the stream body is the single capture owner for an unexpected defect here and preserves an already-reported marker so framework instrumentation does not capture it twice; the route cannot report because it already returned.",
          "Cancellation: browser abort() or component unmount -> request.signal aborts, and/or the platform calls the response body's cancel(reason) -> either path calls ctl.abort(reason) -> the same signal is the one handed to the provider fetch, so the upstream connection actually terminates (a boolean flag or breaking the local loop would not qualify) -> cleanup runs in finally; an AbortError caused by our own ctl produces no error event and no report.",
