          },
          {
            "topic": "Idle timeout",
            "choice": "Sliding timer reset only by provider deltas, owned by the stream channel and expressed inward solely as the signal",
            "rationale": "Bounds provider silence without capping a healthy long stream. Keeping it out of the operation and the port is what prevents the job from inheriting stream liveness semantics; the two channels intentionally use different policies, so no shared named liveness policy is created."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Provider error mapping",
            "choice": "Map provider envelopes to the closed semantic code set inside server/provider/reply-transport.ts; no raw provider text or SDK error as cause on a semantic failure that leaves the adapter",
