          },
          {
            "topic": "Report-once ownership",
            "choice": "Route reports pre-commit, stream body reports post-commit with an already-reported marker, job channel reports for jobs; stream.ts, the operation, and adapters stay silent",
            "rationale": "Each outer channel that can name the request and outcome owns exactly one capture. The marker prevents automatic instrumentation from double-capturing a rethrown exception."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Public surfaces created",
            "choice": "Only stream.ts, job.ts, client.ts — no server.ts, rsc.ts, actions.ts, ui.ts, or query-cache.ts",
            "rationale": "Each surface must have a real consumer and establish a runtime boundary. There is no trusted cross-capability consumer, no RSC read, no mutation, no reused UI, and no TanStack key shared between a server prefetch and a browser query."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Persistence and shared roots",
