          },
          {
            "topic": "HTTP input schema placement",
            "choice": "Request schema stays route-local in app/api/assistant/reply/route.ts; the failure classifier is published from stream.ts",
            "rationale": "Routes own decoding and must not reach into module-private schemas or private application errors; a public classifier belongs on the root contract."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Job entry point",
            "choice": "Queue callback Route Handler with signature verification and durable idempotency, delegating outcome policy to job.ts",
            "rationale": "Service/queue callbacks are a Route Handler use; retries enter there, so idempotency belongs at that boundary while retry/dead-letter classification stays in the capability."
          }
        ],
        "risks": [
          "Keep-alive comment frames must not reset the idle timer, or the timeout is silently disabled — assert in tests that only provider deltas reset it.",
          "Deploy-target behavior (edge/serverless max duration, proxy or CDN buffering) can break streaming independently of this design; pin the route runtime and verify end to end.",
          "If generate-reply.ts holds no real policy it degrades into a forwarding operation; delete it and let both channels call the server adapter instead.",
          "Promoting domain/failure.ts into shared/kernel with only one owning capability would be premature; wait for a second capability with identical meaning and change cadence.",
